# @hub-lanes

# ── DOORBELL COVERAGE (2026-09-16) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Daily at 05:50Z, ten minutes after the CLI sweep: does every repo in
# fleet.conf still have a LIVE webhook pointing at the harness-jobs receiver?
# The doorbell is armed PER REPO (docs/EVENTS.md §4.3 — the org-level hook it
# was designed as answers 403 for our PAT), which means a project onboarded
# after the one-time arming gets none, and a hook someone deletes leaves no
# trace. cromford spent its first day exactly there: zero wakes, triage
# braked to 45-minute ticks, 76 open ai-build issues behind a 5-per-tick
# reconciler, and not one line anywhere saying why. Read-only, one ALERTS line
# per repo per day, and the alert carries the arming command because the shared
# secret is pasted by a human and no script here can read it.
50 5 * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && /root/harness/bin/doorbell-coverage-check.sh --quiet >/dev/null 2>&1
